--- a/docs/cli.rst
+++ b/docs/cli.rst
@@ -1372,6 +1372,21 @@ To disable type detection and treat all columns as TEXT, use ``--no-detect-types
 
     sqlite-utils insert creatures.db creatures creatures.csv --csv --no-detect-types
 
+Use ``--type COLUMN TYPE`` to explicitly set the type of one or more columns.
+The supported types are ``text``, ``integer``, ``float`` and ``blob``. This
+option can be repeated, and explicit types take precedence over automatically
+detected types:
+
+.. code-block:: bash
+
+    sqlite-utils insert creatures.db creatures creatures.csv --csv \
+        --type age text \
+        --type weight float
+
+``--type`` works with both ``insert`` and ``upsert``. It also applies to tables
+that already exist; other columns in an existing table retain their current
+types.
+
